<title>USA: IBM chooses router for server programme.</title>
<headline>IBM chooses router for server programme.</headline>
<dateline>WESTLAKE, Calif 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp (IBM) has chosen a self-contained router made by Sourcecom Corp for its personal computer compatibility programme, Sourcecom said on Monday.</p>
<p>The company said IBM had tested and selected its InCarda self-contained router on a PC-compatible expansion card for its programme.</p>
<p>IBM's programme improves the function of its line of PC servers, it said, adding that it would be designed for small and medium-sized companies that need routing functions.</p>
</text>
